  "aa7fbf51-e7c5-41ac-86f4-be1df00bab2d": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p47-theory",
     "replacement": "**Expected value (mean)**, $E(X)=\\mu$, is the average value of $X$.\n\nDiscrete, with probabilities $P(x)$:\n\n$\\displaystyle E(X)=\\mu=\\sum xP(x)$\n\nContinuous, with PDF $f(x)$ on $[a,b]$:\n\n$\\displaystyle E(X)=\\mu=\\int_a^b xf(x)\\,dx$\n**Variance**, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$, measures spread about the mean. The **standard deviation** is $\\sigma=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{Var}(X)}$.\n\n**Discrete:**\n\n$\\displaystyle \\operatorname{Var}(X)=E(X^2)-\\mu^2=\\sum\\bigl(x^2P(x)\\bigr)-\\mu^2$\n\n**Continuous:**\n\n$\\displaystyle \\operatorname{Var}(X)=E(X^2)-\\mu^2=\\int_a^b x^2f(x)\\,dx-\\mu^2$",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p47-theory",
     "targetFingerprint": "a94b6819914b4079894ea507f8b5ed69f784fbf6c9a381c80f57c87b5c6ab165",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
